1. Architecture & Project Structure

Follow Clean Architecture or MVVM.

Separate layers clearly: domain, data, presentation, core.

Use feature modules for independent features; avoid tight coupling.

Keep core utilities (network, logging, DI, shared components) in a shared module.

Use Dependency Injection (Hilt/Dagger/Koin) to decouple dependencies.

2. UI / UX

Follow Material Design or platform design guidelines.

Keep UI modular: components, widgets, and reusable layouts in a ui module.

Use data binding / view binding to reduce boilerplate.

Prefer compose or modern declarative UI for flexibility (if applicable).

Ensure responsive layouts: support multiple screen sizes and orientations.

3. Networking

Centralize networking logic in a network/data module.

Use Retrofit + OkHttp or equivalent.

Handle errors gracefully: timeouts, offline mode, retries.

Prefer asynchronous calls: Kotlin Coroutines, Flow, or RxJava.

Use HTTPS and secure API communication.

4. Storage & Data Management

Use local DB (Room / SQLDelight) for structured data.

Use DataStore / SharedPreferences for small key-value storage.

Implement caching strategies for offline-first behavior.

Separate entity models (DB) from domain models to avoid leaks.

5. Dependency & Version Management

Maintain a single source of truth for dependencies (e.g., buildSrc or Versions.kt).

Keep Gradle configuration modular and reusable.

Use semantic versioning for modules.

Avoid hardcoding versions in multiple places.

8. Security & Best Practices

Avoid storing sensitive info in plaintext.

Use encrypted storage for secrets or tokens.

Secure network communication (HTTPS, certificate pinning if needed).

Limit exposure of internal modules; keep only necessary APIs public.

9. Performance

Optimize module dependencies to avoid unnecessary builds.

Lazy load features when possible.

Use background threads for heavy work (network, DB, computations).

Avoid memory leaks: lifecycle-aware components, proper cleanup.

Do not hardcode as possible for values. And add core code which would be used in most part of project in core module